#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""tools/gate-manifest: generate and check tools/gate-manifest.json, the step table of the quick gate (PLAN-GATE-2X D2/G2/G3).

  tools/gate-manifest --write     render the manifest from the repo (check-all.sh ALL, shim/build.sh, the wlan/el2 mutant tests, the patch stack) and write it
  tools/gate-manifest --check     exit 1 when the committed file differs from a fresh render, or when the table is incomplete (a step, a build-* variant or a
                                  *_MUTANTS table without a row); wired into the unit step through tools/test_gate_select.py
  tools/gate-manifest --print     the fresh render on stdout

Ceilings (T-cfb7, docs/recipes/port-new-block.md step 8; file tools/gate-manifest-ceilings.json, same "ceiling only lowers" model as tools/doc-ratchet): a block adds at most
ONE shim build variant and ONE mutant table. --check/--write refuse (1) more `build`/`build-*` rows than `build_variants` (a 13th row is a FAIL; fewer than the ceiling is a
FAIL too: lower the number in the same commit, so it can only go down), (2) a `*_MUTANTS` table that is neither in `legacy_mutant_tables` (the 16 that existed before the rule; a
name leaves the list when its table goes, never joins it) nor tagged `# mutant-block: <name>` on the line above it, (3) two tables tagged with the same block name.

One row per step of check-all.sh ALL: lane (A/B/C as in check-all.sh), class, inputs (fnmatch globs of repo files the step reads; an entry may be
{"glob": G, "except": [..]}), budget_s, and where it applies follows / predicate / only. The runtime selector (tools/gate_select.py) only READS the JSON.
class: always = never narrowed by `--quick` and never skipped in any kind: runs whenever one of its inputs changed (validate/rules/public-split: every change);
       quick = runs in `--quick` when an input changed since the base, always in a formal/full gate; formal = full/formal gate only: NEVER selected by its inputs in
       a `--quick` run (the 11 build-* variants after `build`, lint-c; PLAN-GATE-LAYERS s.2 L1: one shim build in the quick lane), added only when a quick run selected every other step.
selector_inputs: a changed file matching one of these globs is the selector's own input: the quick gate runs the FULL set (PLAN-GATE-LAYERS s.3 last row).
run-path tools (RUN_PATH_GLOBS): the only inputs of probe-run / phone-state / hang-recover (PLAN-GATE-LAYERS s.3 row 3), not every tools/* file.
patch_edits (wlan-mutants, mutant-needles): a patch file under xnu/patches that edits a file under one of these prefixes is an input too, judged by its CONTENT at select time
(a patch added after `--write` is not in the static globs; review gate-runfast-1 C2).
`inert` lists the paths no step reads (documentation): a changed file that matches no row input and no inert glob is UNRESOLVED and selects FULL (rule 8).
Last line: RESULT: PASS|FAIL gate-manifest ...  Exit 0/1/2.
"""
